# .gitignore for the public release.
#
# The first section is the one that matters. It is written so that a mistake --
# placing a real data file somewhere in the tree and running ``git add .`` -- does
# not put it into the repository. Everything below it is ordinary hygiene.
#
# The rules below are anchored where they can be, so that a legitimate source file
# is never excluded by accident. In particular nothing here excludes ``*.py``,
# ``*.yaml``, ``*.csv`` under ``data/schema`` or ``data/synthetic``, or the
# expected-output tables under ``examples/``. Those are intended content.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Case-level and restricted data. Never commit any of these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/
data/raw_documents/
data/judgments/
data/private/
data/restricted/
# Case-level tables. Every CSV under data/ is excluded, and the two that are
# intended content are re-included by name. A real case-level table would have to
# be given one of those two names to be tracked, which is a deliberate and visible
# act rather than an oversight.
data/**/*.csv
!data/synthetic/synthetic_cases.csv
!data/schema/data_dictionary.csv
# Judgment documents from which a case could be re-identified.
*.docx
*.doc
*.wps
*.rtf
# Real prediction and feature dumps.
*case_predictions*
*unit_predictions*
*test_predictions*
timeseries_predictions*
*real_shap*
*real_feature_matrix*
*meta_features.parquet
*.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artefacts. The repository ships the code that produces them, not the
# outputs, except for the small tables under examples/ that document expected shape.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/
reports/
experiments/
logs/
*.log
.logs/
# Anything written by a run into a scratch directory.
tmp/
scratch/
scratch_*
*_scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fitted model artefacts. Weights and caches are not distributed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.h5
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.model
# Downloaded model caches.
.cache/
cache/
*.cache
model_cache/
model_weights/
pretrained/
# TabPFN and Hugging Face caches.
tabpfn*/
models--*/
hub/
*.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials*
*credential*.json
*token*.txt
.git-credentials
.netrc
# Local overrides of the path configuration.
config/paths.yaml
config/local.yaml
config/*.local.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environments.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
virtualenv/
conda-meta/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and editor state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.ropeproject/
.spyproject/
.spyderproject/
# Notebook checkpoints. Executed notebooks would carry cell outputs, which can
# contain path and data material, so the checkpoints are not tracked.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system clutter.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
